READ: threshold_freeform is the TRAINING-FREE sliding-window projection (the
paper's own method); per_turn_max is STATELESS (one token at a time, no
sequence); seq_gru/trajectory_mlp are the learned sequence detectors. If the
stateless baseline matches the sequence models, there is no TRAJECTORY signal
on this substrate -- only a per-token one.
CLAIM: a raw AUC is not a result. Two subtractions are mandatory -- 'vs CONF'
(the strongest trivial scalar) and 'vs PROMPT' (a bag-of-words classifier on
the prompt alone). The paper's claim is that decoding-time states beat the
prompt; only the 'vs PROMPT' column can support or refute it.
Screening tier (one model, one layer, one seed; label = prompt class).
